{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"GHSA-5v8v-xvjv-57x7","published":"2026-04-06T09:31:42Z","modified":"2026-07-15T19:01:07.571326237Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-37977"],"summary":"Keycloak vulnerable to information disclosure via CORS header injection due to unvalidated JWT azp claim","details":"A flaw was found in Keycloak. A remote attacker can exploit a Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) header injection vulnerability in Keycloak's User-Managed Access (UMA) token endpoint. This flaw occurs because the `azp` claim from a client-supplied JSON Web Token (JWT) is used to set the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header before the JWT signature is validated. When a specially crafted JWT with an attacker-controlled `azp` value is processed, this value is reflected as the CORS origin, even if the grant is later rejected. This can lead to the exposure of low-sensitivity information from authorization server error responses, weakening origin isolation, but only when a target client is misconfigured with `webOrigins: [\"*\"]`.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"org.keycloak:keycloak-services","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.keycloak/keycloak-services"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"26.4.13"}]}],"versions":["1.0-alpha-1","1.0-alpha-1-12062013","1.0-alpha-2","1.0-alpha-3","1.0-alpha-4","1.0-beta-1","1.0-beta-1-20150521","1.0-beta-1-20150523","1.0-beta-2","1.0-beta-3","1.0-beta-4","1.0-final","1.0-rc-1","1.0-rc-2","1.0.1.Final","1.0.2.Final","1.0.3.Final","1.0.4.Final","1.0.5.Final","1.1.0.Beta1","1.1.0.Beta2","1.1.0.Final","1.1.1.Final","1.2.0.Beta1","1.2.0.CR1","1.2.0.Final","1.3.0.Final","1.3.1.Final","1.4.0.Final","1.5.0-Final","1.5.0.Final","1.5.1.Final","1.6.0.Final","1.6.1.Final","1.7.0.CR1","1.7.0.Final","1.8.0.Alpha1","1.8.0.CR1","1.8.0.CR2","1.8.0.CR3","1.8.0.Final","1.8.1.Final","1.9.0.CR1","1.9.0.Final","1.9.1.Final","1.9.2.Final","1.9.3.Final","1.9.4.Final","1.9.5.Final","1.9.7.Final","1.9.8.Final","10.0.0","10.0.1","10.0.2","